🔹 STEP 28 — API Security Controls
1. Install Security Packages
Run inside:
cd /home/nix/u01/blockchain-integration/blockchain-api
Install:
npm install helmet cors express-rate-limit hpp express-validator

2. Update .env
Open:
nano .env
Add or update:
# ==================================================# STEP 28 — API SECURITY CONTROLS# ==================================================# Request body size limitREQUEST_BODY_LIMIT=1mb# Allowed CORS origins - comma separatedCORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200,http://127.0.0.1:4200,http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1:8080# Rate limitRATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=900000RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=100# Stricter limits for auth endpointsAUTH_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=900000AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=10# Internal service API keyINTERNAL_API_KEY=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_LONG_RANDOM_SECRET_VALUE# Enable or disable API key check for service routesENABLE_API_KEY_PROTECTION=true# Security loggingENABLE_SUSPICIOUS_REQUEST_LOGGING=true
Generate a strong key:
openssl rand -hex 32
Then replace:
INTERNAL_API_KEY=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_LONG_RANDOM_SECRET_VALUE
Example:
INTERNAL_API_KEY=8f1e9c5a64bdb8f5a1f4938a7c9efc81e17931cc5c7bcb8e3c3a6e42f9b0aa1d

